<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jan van Riebeeck</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1619">1619</a>–<a href="/years/1677">1677</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jan van Riebeeck was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a> official who landed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/table-bay">Table Bay</a> in 1652 to set up a station supplying fresh food to ships sailing to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-indies">East Indies</a>, the beginning of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-town">Cape Town</a>. He commanded the Cape until 1662, when he became governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malacca">Malacca</a> until 1665. He later served as secretary of the Company's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/council-of-the-indies">Council of the Indies</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/batavia">Batavia</a>, where he died.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jan-van-riebeeck.jpg" alt="Jan van Riebeeck" width="320" height="435" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: anonymous · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portret_van_Jan_van_Riebeeck_(1619-77)._Bevelhebber_van_Kaap_de_Goede_Hoop_en_van_Malacca_en_secretaris_van_de_Hoge_Regering_van_Batavia,_SK-A-805.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The Cape Colony, established in 1652 by <b>Jan van Riebeeck</b> as a VOC resupply station, produced the Afrikaner settler community whose descendants shaped South African history into the twentieth century.</blockquote><a href="/empire/dutch-empire">Dutch Empire · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Jan van Riebeeck</b> reached Table Bay to set up a supply station for the Dutch East India Company.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/april-6">6 April in history</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1652 <b>Jan van Riebeeck</b> landed at Table Bay to set up a refreshment station for VOC ships sailing to the East Indies.</blockquote><a href="/state/dutch-cape-colony">Dutch Cape Colony</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Jan van Riebeeck</b>, founder of Cape Town, governed it from 1662 to 1665.</blockquote><a href="/state/dutch-malacca">Dutch Malacca</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Culemborg, in what is now <a href="/countries/netherlands">the Netherlands</a>. Died in Batavia, in what is now <a href="/countries/indonesia">Indonesia</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=51.95,5.23&amp;year=1656" aria-label="Culemborg on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4668 368 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Jan van Riebeeck"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5118 638h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5118 638h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=51.95,5.23&amp;year=1656">What was here in 1656? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
